- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: Your `QuestLog` class is doing too much; it's responsible for managing quests and also formatting their display. Apply the Single Responsibility Principle by extracting the display logic into a new, dedicated class.

Current code in the editor:
```
class QuestLog {
    constructor() {
        this.activeQuests = [];
    }

    addQuest(questName) {
        this.activeQuests.push({ name: questName, completed: false });
    }

    completeQuest(questName) {
        const quest = this.activeQuests.find(q => q.name === questName);
        if (quest) {
            quest.completed = true;
        }
    }

    // TODO: This method combines quest management with display logic, violating SRP.
    // Extract the logic for generating the summary string into a *new* class.
    // The QuestLog should only provide the raw quest data, not format it.
    getQuestSummary() {
        if (this.activeQuests.length === 0) {
            return "No active quests.";
        }
        let summary = "--- Current Quests ---\n";
        this.activeQuests.forEach(quest => {
            summary += `- ${quest.name} [${quest.completed ? "COMPLETED" : "ACTIVE"}]\n`;
        });
        return summary;
    }
}

const log = new QuestLog();
log.addQuest("Defeat the Dragon");
log.addQuest("Find the Ancient Relic");
log.completeQuest("Defeat the Dragon");

console.log(log.getQuestSummary()); // This call needs to be updated after refactoring
```

